  "worked_solution": "A function $\u03c8(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if the following equations hold:\n\n$$\nP=\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202y},\\,Q=-\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202x}\n$$\n\nComputing the partial derivatives of the function $\u03c8(x,y),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y-x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y, \\\\ Q & =-\\frac{\u2202\u03c8}{\u2202x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y-x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field with the stream function $\u03c8(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y-x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & =P\\,i+Q\\,j \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061y\\,i+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061y+1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
